1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,362
Hello!

2
00:00:00,362 --> 00:00:03,195
Today we spend a day at Hyeopjae Beach in Jeju.

3
00:00:03,195 --> 00:00:08,740
From waking up in the morning to falling asleep at night — let's describe our day in Korean!

4
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:15,456
'일과' [il-gwa] means daily routine — the things you do every day.

5
00:00:15,456 --> 00:00:17,510
Today we learn them in order.

6
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:20,077
Key word!

7
00:00:20,077 --> 00:00:24,030
'일어나다' [il-eo-na-da] — to wake up, to get up from sleep.

8
00:00:25,440 --> 00:00:30,709
'아침에 일어나요' [a-chim-e-il-eo-na-yo] (I wake up in the morning).

9
00:00:30,709 --> 00:00:35,979
'-에' [--e] marks time: 아침에 (in the morning),

10
00:00:35,979 --> 00:00:37,920
밤에 (at night).

11
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:42,268
Ask '몇 시에 일어나요' [myeot-si-e-il-eo-na-yo]? (What time do you get up? ).

12
00:00:42,268 --> 00:00:44,780
A great conversation starter.

13
00:00:45,230 --> 00:00:48,457
'일곱 시에 일어나요' [il-gop-si-e-il-eo-na-yo] (I get up at seven).

14
00:00:48,457 --> 00:00:50,510
Answer with the time.

15
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:55,697
'일찍' [il-jjik] (early) and '늦게' [neut-ge] (late).

16
00:00:55,697 --> 00:01:01,740
Learn them as a pair: 일찍 일어나요, 늦게 자요.

17
00:01:02,190 --> 00:01:04,723
'창문을 열어요' [chang-mun-eul-yeol-eo-yo] (I open the window).

18
00:01:04,723 --> 00:01:06,919
Wow — the sea at Hyeopjae!

19
00:01:06,919 --> 00:01:09,030
And what a beautiful sky.

20
00:01:10,990 --> 00:01:15,860
'세수하다' [se-su-ha-da] means to wash your face — the first thing in the morning.

21
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:20,942
'이를 닦다' [i-reul-dak-da] (to brush your teeth).

22
00:01:20,942 --> 00:01:23,710
Clean them well with a toothbrush.

23
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:27,127
'옷을 입다' [ot-eul-ip-da] (to put on clothes).

24
00:01:27,127 --> 00:01:31,154
The opposite is '옷을 벗다' [ot-eul-beot-da] (to take off).

25
00:01:31,154 --> 00:01:33,380
Learn them as a pair.

26
00:01:37,090 --> 00:01:45,150
Use these to connect your routine: '세수하고 그다음에 아침을 먹어요' (I wash my face and then eat breakfast).

27
00:01:45,630 --> 00:01:50,661
'아침을 먹다' [a-chim-eul-meok-da] (to eat breakfast).

28
00:01:50,661 --> 00:01:56,770
아침/점심/저녁 + 먹다 — three meals a day.

29
00:01:57,220 --> 00:02:00,401
'마시다' [ma-si-da] is for liquids.

30
00:02:00,401 --> 00:02:07,520
Korean distinguishes 먹다 (eat) from 마시다 (drink).

31
00:02:07,970 --> 00:02:11,802
Uh-oh — look at the clock! '늦었어요' [neut-eot-eo-yo] (We're late).

32
00:02:11,802 --> 00:02:14,330
And we have to get to the cafe!

33
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:19,530
'서두르다' [seo-du-reu-da] means to hurry. Let's move quickly!

34
00:02:21,450 --> 00:02:24,980
Key word! '일하다' [il-ha-da] — to work.

35
00:02:27,610 --> 00:02:35,700
'-에서' [--e-seo] marks the place where an action happens: 카페에서 (at a cafe),

36
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:37,470
집에서 (at home).

37
00:02:39,390 --> 00:02:42,317
Key word! '공부하다' [gong-bu-ha-da] — to study.

38
00:02:42,317 --> 00:02:44,930
I study Korean every day.

39
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:53,303
'을/를' [eul-/-reul] marks the object: 한국어를 공부해요 (I study Korean),

40
00:02:53,303 --> 00:02:56,660
책을 읽어요 (I read a book).

41
00:02:57,110 --> 00:03:01,910
'책을 읽다' [chaek-eul-il-da] (to read a book). Sit quietly and read.

42
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:06,850
'쓰다' [sseu-da] means to write. Write it in your notebook.

43
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:11,183
'점심을 먹다' [jeom-sim-eul-meok-da] (to eat lunch).

44
00:03:11,183 --> 00:03:15,020
Eating lunch with a sea view — the best!

45
00:03:15,930 --> 00:03:19,543
Wait — look at the sky! '구름' [gu-reum] (clouds).

46
00:03:19,543 --> 00:03:21,350
They are beautiful.

47
00:03:22,260 --> 00:03:26,920
'쉬다' [swi-da] means to rest — to stop working and relax.

48
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:33,443
'일하고 나서 쉬어요' [il-ha-go-na-seo-swi-eo-yo] (I rest after working).

49
00:03:33,443 --> 00:03:37,180
'-고 나서' [--go-na-seo] shows the order of actions.

50
00:03:37,630 --> 00:03:40,718
'산책하다' [san-chaek-ha-da] — to take a leisurely walk.

51
00:03:40,718 --> 00:03:43,170
Let's walk along the beach.

52
00:03:44,750 --> 00:03:47,548
'해변을 걸어요' [hae-byeon-eul-geol-eo-yo] (I walk on the beach).

53
00:03:47,548 --> 00:03:50,870
The white sand at Hyeopjae is so soft.

54
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:56,380
'수영하다' [su-yeong-ha-da] (to swim). Let's swim in the emerald water!

55
00:03:56,830 --> 00:03:59,304
'사진을 찍다' [sa-jin-eul-jjik-da] (to take a photo).

56
00:03:59,304 --> 00:04:02,970
One shot with Biyangdo Island behind us!

57
00:04:03,420 --> 00:04:07,810
'재미있어요' [jae-mi-it-eo-yo]! (It's fun! ). What a great day.

58
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:12,750
After all that play — '피곤해요' [pi-gon-hae-yo] (I'm tired).

59
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:19,080
'저녁을 먹다' [jeo-nyeok-eul-meok-da] (to eat dinner) — the last meal of the day.

60
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:23,679
'자기 전에 씻어요' [ja-gi-jeon-e-ssit-eo-yo] (I wash before sleeping).

61
00:04:23,679 --> 00:04:27,380
'-기 전에' [--gi-jeon-e] = before doing something.

62
00:04:27,830 --> 00:04:32,340
'저녁을 먹은 후에 산책해요' (I walk after dinner).

63
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:36,040
'-ㄴ 후에' [--n-hu-e] = after doing something.

64
00:04:36,490 --> 00:04:37,993
'전화하다' [jeon-hwa-ha-da] (to call).

65
00:04:37,993 --> 00:04:42,060
Call your family and tell them about your day.

66
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:50,670
'보다' [bo-da] means to watch/see. 텔레비전을 봐요 (I watch TV).

67
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:53,849
'노을을 보다' [no-eul-eul-bo-da] (to watch the sunset).

68
00:04:53,849 --> 00:04:56,930
The sunset at Hyeopjae is stunning.

69
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:59,755
'아름다워요' [a-reum-da-wo-yo] (It's beautiful).

70
00:04:59,755 --> 00:05:02,320
The whole sky turns orange.

71
00:05:04,690 --> 00:05:09,710
'샤워하다' [sya-wo-ha-da] (to take a shower). Wash up before bed.

72
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:12,465
'일기를 쓰다' [il-gi-reul-sseu-da] (to write a diary).

73
00:05:12,465 --> 00:05:15,510
Write about your day — a great habit.

74
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:22,040
Wait — the sky is full of '별' [byeol] (stars)!

75
00:05:22,490 --> 00:05:26,745
Sitting on the '모래' [mo-rae] (sand), watching the stars.

76
00:05:26,745 --> 00:05:29,280
What a lovely day it's been.

77
00:05:29,730 --> 00:05:34,460
Key word! '자다' [ja-da] — to sleep. The end of the day.

78
00:05:34,910 --> 00:05:40,421
'열한 시에 자요' [yeol-han-si-e-ja-yo] (I sleep at eleven). Time + 자다.

79
00:05:40,421 --> 00:05:42,520
The day is done.

80
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:48,985
Let's review: 일어나다 (wake up), 일하다 (work),

81
00:05:48,985 --> 00:05:55,510
공부하다 (study), 자다 (sleep). How about your day?

82
00:05:55,510 --> 00:06:00,730
Tell us in the comments. Good night!

